From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:37:15 +0100
Subject: drm/sun4i: hdmi: audio: release the DMA channel on destroy

sun4i_hdmi_audio_destroy() runs at every encoder disable. It calls
snd_soc_unregister_component(dev), which removes all components of the
device, the dmaengine PCM one included (unregistering by the DAI
component driver would not help: it has no name, so the lookup matches
every component of the device as well), and only then
snd_dmaengine_pcm_unregister(), which no longer finds its component and
returns without releasing the DMA channel. Every following enable
requests another channel ("sysfs: cannot create duplicate filename
.../dma:audio-tx" with a stack dump): one channel leaks per
disable/enable cycle (modeset, DPMS off/on).

Unregister the PCM first, then the remaining DAI component. Same in the
error path of sun4i_hdmi_audio_create().

Tested on a Rikomagic MK802 (A10, 1 GiB) with a 6.18.56 kernel built by
the Armbian framework with this change as a userpatch: one DMA channel
after five DPMS off/on cycles, no warnings, HDMI audio still opens; a
build without it held four channels after three cycles. The order bug is
not SoC specific, but it was seen on the A10 only; HDMI audio was not
tested on the A20.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_hdmi_audio.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_hdmi_audio.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_hdmi_audio.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_hdmi_audio.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_hdmi_audio.c
@@ -424,7 +424,9 @@ int sun4i_hdmi_audio_create(struct sun4i_hdmi *hdmi)
 	return 0;
 
 unregister_component:
+	snd_dmaengine_pcm_unregister(hdmi->dev);
 	snd_soc_unregister_component(hdmi->dev);
+	return ret;
 unregister_pcm:
 	snd_dmaengine_pcm_unregister(hdmi->dev);
 	return ret;
@@ -443,8 +445,13 @@ void sun4i_hdmi_audio_destroy(struct sun4i_hdmi *hdmi)
 	data = snd_soc_card_get_drvdata(card);
 
 	snd_soc_unregister_card(card);
-	snd_soc_unregister_component(hdmi->dev);
+	/*
+	 * The PCM first: snd_soc_unregister_component() removes every component
+	 * of the device, after which snd_dmaengine_pcm_unregister() no longer
+	 * finds its own and never releases the DMA channel.
+	 */
 	snd_dmaengine_pcm_unregister(hdmi->dev);
+	snd_soc_unregister_component(hdmi->dev);
 
 	dev_set_drvdata(hdmi->dev, data);
 }
